{"path":"numeric/complex/sqrt","title":"std::sqrt(std::complex)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>sqrt<small>(std::complex)</small>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/complex/sqrt","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes the square root of the complex number z with a branch cut along the negative real axis.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> sqrt<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes the square root of the complex number <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> with a branch cut along the negative real axis.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> complex number to take the square root of\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, returns the square root of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>, in the range of the right half-plane, including the imaginary axis (<span class=\"texhtml\">[0; +∞)</span> along the real axis and <span class=\"texhtml\">(−∞; +∞)</span> along the imaginary axis).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Error_handling_and_special_values\">Error handling and special values</h3>\n<p>Errors are reported consistent with <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/math_errhandling\">math_errhandling</a></span>.\n</p><p>If the implementation supports IEEE floating-point arithmetic,\n</p>\n<ul><li> The function is continuous onto the branch cut taking into account the sign of imaginary part\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sqrt\"><span class=\"kw1337\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sqrt</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conj</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/conj\"><span class=\"kw2708\">std::<span class=\"me2\">conj</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sqrt\"><span class=\"kw1337\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sqrt</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(±0,+0)</code>, the result is <code>(+0,+0)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(x,+∞)</code>, the result is <code>(+∞,+∞)</code> even if x is NaN\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(x,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> (unless x is ±∞) and  <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(-∞,y)</code>, the result is <code>(+0,+∞)</code> for finite positive y\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,y)</code>, the result is <code>(+∞,+0)</code> for finite positive y\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(-∞,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,∞)</code> (sign of imaginary part unspecified)\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(+∞,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(+∞,NaN)</code>\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,y)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/fenv/FE_exceptions\">FE_INVALID</a></span> may be raised\n</li><li> If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code>, the result is <code>(NaN,NaN)</code>\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The semantics of this function are intended to be consistent with the C function <a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/csqrt\"><code>csqrt</code></a>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Square root of -4 is \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sqrt\"><span class=\"kw1337\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sqrt</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">4.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Square root of (-4,-0) is \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sqrt\"><span class=\"kw1337\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sqrt</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">4.0</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (the other side of the cut)<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Square root of -4 is (0,2)\nSquare root of (-4,-0) is (0,-2) (the other side of the cut)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2597\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2597</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td>specification mishandles signed zero imaginary parts\n</td>\n<td>erroneous requirement removed\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/pow\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>pow<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  complex power, one or both arguments may be a complex number <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sqrt\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sqrt</span><span>sqrtf</span><span>sqrtl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes square root (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small{\\sqrt{x}}\"><span class=\"t-mrad\"><span>√</span><span>x</span></span></span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/sqrt\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sqrt<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sqrt\">std::sqrt</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/csqrt\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>csqrt</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Error handling and special values","id":"Error_handling_and_special_values"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::sqrt(std::complex)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Computes the square root of the complex number z with a branch cut along the negative real axis."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, returns the square root of z, in the range of the right half-plane, including the imaginary axis ([0; +∞) along the real axis and (−∞; +∞)…"},{"label":"Error handling and special values","note":"Errors are reported consistent with math_errhandling."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The semantics of this function are intended to be consistent with the C function csqrt."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"pow(std::complex)","note":"complex power, one or both arguments may be a complex number"},{"label":"sqrt, sqrtf, sqrtl","note":"computes square root (√x)"},{"label":"sqrt(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::sqrt to each element of valarray"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":367,"codeBlockCount":2}
